---
title: "Filters"
description: "Compose QQL comparisons, logical predicates, text, nested, ID, vector, count, and geo filters."
sidebar:
  order: 3
---

`WHERE` lowers to a Qdrant filter on REST, gRPC, and edge backends.

## Scalar and logical filters

{% qqlExample title="Comparisons and boolean logic" %}
QUERY TEXT 'search' FROM docs
WHERE status = 'published'
  AND year BETWEEN 2024 AND 2026
  AND tags NOT IN ('archived', 'private')
  AND (score >= 0.7 OR featured = true)
LIMIT 10;
{% /qqlExample %}

Supported forms include comparison operators, `BETWEEN`, `IN`, null/empty
checks, `MATCH`, `NESTED`, `HAS_VECTOR`, `VALUES_COUNT`, and geo predicates.
Precedence is predicate → `NOT` → `AND` → `OR`.

## Text and nested filters

{% qqlExample title="Text and nested payloads" %}
QUERY TEXT 'quality' FROM products
WHERE description MATCH PHRASE 'machine washable'
  AND NESTED('reviews', rating >= 4 AND verified = true)
LIMIT 20;
{% /qqlExample %}

## Geo filters

{% qqlExample title="Radius filter" %}
QUERY TEXT 'coffee' FROM places
WHERE location GEO_RADIUS {
  center: {lat: 52.52, lon: 13.405},
  radius: 1500.0
}
LIMIT 10;
{% /qqlExample %}

Latitude, longitude, radius, and polygon shapes are validated before planning.

{% aside type="caution" title="Routing is not a filter" %}
`SHARD 'acme'` is a request-level `ShardKeySelector`. It never appears inside
the Qdrant filter. Use a tenant predicate or `inject_filter` for isolation.
{% /aside %}
